## 7. Technology

- **HTML + CSS + vanilla JavaScript (ES modules)**. No build tools, no npm, no bundler, no framework.
- **Firebase Firestore** via the modular SDK from the CDN (pin the version):
  `https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.1/firebase-app.js` and `.../firebase-firestore.js`
- **Vercel-compatible**: static site, `index.html` at the project root. Add `vercel.json` only if needed (e.g., no special config required for hash routing).

### File structure
```
/index.html
/css/styles.css
/js/app.js                 // router, state, role + theme handling
/js/firebase.js            // Firebase init + small helper functions (getAll, getOne, save, update)
/js/grading.js             // calculateTotal(), getGrade(), validateWeights(), validateBands()
/js/ui.js                  // render helpers: cards, list rows, badges, toast, modal
/js/screens/*.js           // one file per screen (dashboard, positions, form, detail, evaluate, employees, settings)
/js/data/titles.js         // departments + job titles (Section 11 of this file)
/js/data/formConfig.js     // sections and fields (Section 5.3 of this file)
/js/data/labels.js         // all Azerbaijani UI texts (statuses, buttons, errors)
/js/data/seed.js           // sample data (Section 5.5 of this file)
/fonts/                    // empty; optional Hilton Sans files
/SPEC.md
```

### Firebase setup
- `firebase.js` contains a `firebaseConfig` object with placeholders (`apiKey: "YOUR_API_KEY"` …). Show a clear console message and a UI message in Azerbaijani if the config is not filled: "Firebase konfiqurasiyası doldurulmayıb."
- MVP Firestore rules (demo only, with a README note that real Authentication + role rules are required before production):
```
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if true; }
  }
}
```
- Do not use realtime listeners; use simple `getDocs` / `getDoc` and reload the list after each save.

### Code rules
- Keep functions small, with short comments in English.
- Escape user text before inserting into HTML (avoid XSS).
- All UI texts come from `labels.js` or `formConfig.js`. No hard-coded English in the UI.
- Format dates as `DD.MM.YYYY` in the UI, ISO in the database.
- Write a short `README.md` with: how to create the Firebase project, where to paste the config, how to run locally (`npx serve` or opening a local server), how to deploy to Vercel.

### 45-minute build order (suggested)
1. (5 min) Project files, CSS variables, light/dark toggle, layout, router.
2. (5 min) `firebase.js`, `grading.js`, `labels.js`, `titles.js`, `formConfig.js`, `seed.js`.
3. (10 min) Position list (card/list, search, filters) + dashboard.
4. (10 min) Position form wizard (generated from `formConfig.js`) + detail screen.
5. (8 min) Evaluation screen + approval flow + role permissions.
6. (4 min) Employees + Settings + seed button.
7. (3 min) Test using the checklist in Section 8.

